+<section class="section reading-wrap" id="release">
+  <h2>Code, models, and reproducible inference</h2>
+  <p>The release is being prepared. The model and processed-test repositories below may require access until publication.</p>
+  <p><a class="pill" href="https://huggingface.co/human-motion-capture/AnyMo" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Models on Hugging Face</a>
+  <a class="pill" href="https://huggingface.co/datasets/human-motion-capture/processed_test_dataset_of_AnyMo" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Processed test assets</a>
+  <a class="pill" href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2605.29488" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Paper and citation</a></p>
+  <p>The prepared code includes text and trajectory inference with the released 3B checkpoint. Optional latent fitting improves pelvis-path tracking while keeping model weights fixed; foot contact is not explicitly constrained.</p>
+  <pre><code>python tools/infer.py \
+  --checkpoint work_dirs/anymo_stage_3_3B_210e_48gpu/lite_epoch_210.pth \
+  --prompt "A person turns their body while swinging both arms." \
+  --trajectory trajectory.npy --tta-steps 400</code></pre>
+  <p class="small-note">Inputs use pelvis XYZ in meters, Y-up, at30fps. Dataset previews elsewhere on this page are real dataset motion; they are not AnyMo-generated results. Consult the code README for installation, normalization and release status.</p>
+</section>
